WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:22.980
Shortly after the mayor left for Arras, Fantine awoke. She had passed a long, difficult night.

2
00:00:22.981 --> 00:00:29.051
"How are you this morning?" asked Sister Simplice, one of two nuns who worked at the infirmary.

3
00:00:29.052 --> 00:00:33.393
"I want to see Mayor Madeleine," Fantine said weakly.

4
00:00:33.394 --> 00:00:40.202
"Later," said Sister Simplice. "You know he comes to visit you every day promptly at three o'clock."

5
00:00:40.203 --> 00:00:48.639
Fantine rested for the next several hours, but by two thirty she was agitated and kept asking Sister Simplice the time.

6
00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:56.853
The clock struck three. Fantine, who was usually too weak to turn over in bed, sat up and looked at the door.

7
00:00:56.854 --> 00:01:05.281
Nobody came in; the door did not open. Finally after 15 minutes of anticipation, Fantine lay down.

8
00:01:05.282 --> 00:01:09.678
Sister Simplice was surprised that the mayor was late.

9
00:01:09.679 --> 00:01:16.432
At six o'clock she sent a servant to the factory to ask if the mayor would soon be coming to the infirmary.

10
00:01:16.433 --> 00:01:22.241
The servant returned and reported that Madeleine had left by carriage early that morning.

11
00:01:22.242 --> 00:01:29.083
"I can hear you talking about Mayor Madeleine!" Fantine called out. "Why hasn't he come?"

12
00:01:29.084 --> 00:01:32.916
"He has gone away," said Sister Simplice.

13
00:01:32.917 --> 00:01:42.242
Fantine sprang up and sat on the edge of her bed. "He must have gone to fetch Cosette! I think they'll be back by tomorrow, don't you?"

14
00:01:42.243 --> 00:01:52.821
Sister Simplice did not contradict Fantine but helped her back under the covers. "You are very sick, my child. Try to rest and don't talk."

15
00:01:52.822 --> 00:02:03.075
Fantine fell asleep with a smile on her face. The doctor arrived at about eight o'clock, and Fantine opened her eyes as he took her pulse.

16
00:02:03.076 --> 00:02:11.384
"Oh, there's no need for that," she said. "I'm cured! Cosette is coming tomorrow!"

17
00:02:11.385 --> 00:02:15.964
The doctor was surprised to find that Fantine really did appear to be better.

18
00:02:15.965 --> 00:02:22.305
Her pulse was stronger, and new life seemed to flow through the seriously ill young woman.

19
00:02:22.306 --> 00:02:30.123
As the doctor left, he said to Sister Simplice, "If the mayor does bring Cosette tomorrow, who knows what will happen?

20
00:02:30.124 --> 00:02:35.702
I've seen happiness cure some people, and perhaps it will do so in this case."

21
00:02:35.703 --> 00:02:40.115
Meanwhile the mayor had finally reached Arras at eight o'clock that night.

22
00:02:40.116 --> 00:02:47.282
The lights were still on in the courthouse, so he went inside. A police officer stood near the closed door of the courtroom.

23
00:02:47.283 --> 00:02:51.463
"You can't go in, monsieur," said the policeman. "The courtroom is full."

24
00:02:51.464 --> 00:02:54.353
"What? There are no more seats?"

25
00:02:54.354 --> 00:03:01.861
The policeman hesitated. "There are some seats behind the judge, but he only allows public officials to sit there."

26
00:03:01.862 --> 00:03:08.012
Madeleine crossed the hall and went slowly down the stairs. He seemed to hesitate on every step.

27
00:03:08.013 --> 00:03:13.529
When he reached the landing, he stopped and wrote Mayor Madeleine on a piece of paper.

28
00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:17.155
Then he went back and handed this paper to the policeman.

29
00:03:17.156 --> 00:03:21.409
"Take that to the judge," said the mayor in a commanding voice.

30
00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:27.488
The policeman showed the paper to the judge and whispered, "This gentleman would like to witness the trial."

31
00:03:27.489 --> 00:03:36.401
The judge was familiar with Mayor Madeleine's name and knew that he was universally admired. "Allow him to enter," said the judge.

32
00:03:36.402 --> 00:03:42.314
A few minutes later Madeleine followed the policeman into the courtroom and took a seat behind the judge.

33
00:03:42.315 --> 00:03:51.806
Terrified that someone might see him, he slouched behind a pile of the judge's papers, where he was still able to view most of the courtroom.

34
00:03:51.807 --> 00:03:58.631
He noticed that Monsieur Bamatabois, who had thrown the snow at Fantine, was one of the jurors.

35
00:03:58.632 --> 00:04:06.703
Madeleine stared at the accused man, Champmathieu. He felt as if he were looking at an older version of himself.

36
00:04:06.704 --> 00:04:13.536
There was definitely a resemblance between the two men. The prosecuting attorney started questioning Champmathieu.

37
00:04:13.537 --> 00:04:19.036
"First, did you climb the wall, break off the tree branch, and steal the apples?

38
00:04:19.037 --> 00:04:24.878
And second, are you the former convict known as Jean Valjean?"

39
00:04:24.879 --> 00:04:28.346
"I never stole anything!" said Champmathieu.

40
00:04:28.347 --> 00:04:34.195
"I found the broken branch on the ground and picked it up, little knowing what trouble it would cause me.

41
00:04:34.196 --> 00:04:41.608
You talk about someone named Jean Valjean, but I don't know who that is. My name is Champmathieu."

42
00:04:41.609 --> 00:04:44.584
The prosecuting attorney addressed the judge.

43
00:04:44.585 --> 00:04:54.838
"Since the accused man is denying the charges, we request that you call the convicts, Brevet, Cochepaille, and Chenildieu, to the witness stand.

44
00:04:54.839 --> 00:05:01.425
I would like to ask them—as well as the police officer Javert—to identify this man."

45
00:05:01.426 --> 00:05:08.228
"As you recall," said the judge, "we gave Javert permission to leave after he made his statement.

46
00:05:08.229 --> 00:05:10.497
But I will call the others."

47
00:05:10.498 --> 00:05:16.842
The three convicts were led into the courtroom, and the judge asked each of them to identify the accused man.

48
00:05:16.843 --> 00:05:20.473
The convicts were all certain that the man was Jean Valjean.

49
00:05:20.474 --> 00:05:28.648
"Prisoner, you have listened to these men identify you as Jean Valjean," said the judge. "What do you have to say?"

50
00:05:28.649 --> 00:05:36.791
The confused old man simply laughed. A buzz of noise filled the courtroom as the spectators started talking.

51
00:05:36.792 --> 00:05:41.323
It was obvious that Champmathieu was going to be found guilty.

52
00:05:41.324 --> 00:05:47.727
"Officers, enforce order in the court!" said the judge. "I'm about to sum up the case."

53
00:05:47.728 --> 00:05:50.553
At this moment there was a movement near the judge.

54
00:05:50.554 --> 00:06:00.871
Mayor Madeleine slowly stood up and walked to the center of the courtroom. "Brevet, Chenildieu, and Cochepaille, look at me!"

55
00:06:00.872 --> 00:06:08.371
The judge, Monsieur Bamatabois, and a dozen other people in the courtroom all exclaimed at once, "Mayor Madeleine!"

56
00:06:08.372 --> 00:06:12.153
"Don't you recognize me?" he said to the three prisoners.

57
00:06:12.154 --> 00:06:17.601
All three looked confused and indicated with a shake of the head that they did not know him.

58
00:06:17.602 --> 00:06:24.776
Madeleine turned toward the judge. "Your Honor, release the accused man and order my arrest.

59
00:06:24.777 --> 00:06:30.434
He is not the man whom you seek because I am Jean Valjean."

60
00:06:30.435 --> 00:06:33.427
The courtroom went totally silent.

61
00:06:33.428 --> 00:06:40.665
The judge gave the mayor a look of pity. "Is there a doctor here? Mayor Madeleine appears to be ill."

62
00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:44.681
"Thank you, Your Honor," said the mayor, "but I am not ill.

63
00:06:44.682 --> 00:06:52.927
You were on the verge of making a huge mistake, and I will prove it to you." Then Madeleine turned back to the three convicts.

64
00:06:52.928 --> 00:06:58.054
"Brevet, do you remember those checkered knit suspenders you always wore on the prison ship?"

65
00:06:58.055 --> 00:07:00.922
Brevet started as if struck by lightning.

66
00:07:00.923 --> 00:07:06.570
"Chenildieu," said the mayor, "you have a large scar on your left shoulder, don't you?"

67
00:07:06.571 --> 00:07:09.118
"That's true!" exclaimed Chenildieu.

68
00:07:09.119 --> 00:07:16.657
"And, Cochepaille, you have a blue tattoo on your left arm with the date March 1, 1815."

69
00:07:16.658 --> 00:07:21.125
Cochepaille rolled up his sleeve and revealed the tattoo.

70
00:07:21.126 --> 00:07:24.712
The unhappy mayor addressed the entire courtroom.

71
00:07:24.713 --> 00:07:31.712
"You can clearly see that I am Jean Valjean, and I admit that I robbed the chimney sweep Little Gervais."

72
00:07:31.713 --> 00:07:36.641
He gave a smile of triumph, but it was also a smile of despair.

73
00:07:36.642 --> 00:07:41.458
Everyone in the courtroom was stunned, and no one seemed to know what to do.

74
00:07:41.459 --> 00:07:45.442
"I won't disturb this trial anymore," continued Valjean.

75
00:07:45.443 --> 00:07:49.615
"I am leaving because I have not been arrested, and I have many things to do.

76
00:07:49.616 --> 00:07:56.107
The prosecuting attorney knows who I am and where I live, so he'll have me arrested when he chooses."

77
00:07:56.108 --> 00:08:03.679
Valjean left the courtroom, and less than an hour later, all charges were dropped against Champmathieu.
